		"viz_8GXsmgjV": {
			"cornerRadius": [
				10,
				10,
				10,
				10
			],
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "#fbf4ff",
				"fontColor": "#000000",
				"fontFamily": "Helvetica",
				"markdown": "# Analyze capacity reservations on compute costs\n`#Allocation`  `#Reporting & Analytics` `#Forecasting`  `#Workload Optimization` `#Architecting for Cloud`  `#Onboarding Workload`\n### Context\nCompute costs are often the highest spend area in a cloud bill, it may be useful for FinOps practitioners and Engineers to understand the volume of costs that are coming from reserved commitments either used or unused compared to the amount of compute costs that have no reservations applied. Capacity reservations can be very useful for Engineering to help them ensure capacity is available for their services when it is needed, **however when reducing usage and rightsizing workloads capacity reservations need to be adjusted at the same time**.\n### FOCUS Columns\n\n- Charge Period Start \n- Charge Period End \n- Billed Cost \n- Effective Cost \n- Service Category \n- Provider \n- Billing Account ID"
			},
			"type": "splunk.markdown"
		},
